On 8/30/24 4:19 AM, Thomas Nicholson wrote:
> but the $cov.x matrix of non-latent variables contains
> all 0s.

That is to be expected. The 'cov.x' matrix only contains the exogenous
covariates, and their covariance matrix is (usually) saturated. As a
result, the residuals will be zero.

Yves.

