On 9/9/24 12:14 AM, Thomas Nicholson wrote:
> Thanks Yves, that does make sense. Interesting that I do get non-zero
> values with MLR estimation which I think is initially what threw me.

One difference is that in the categorical case, lavaan (per default)
switches to conditional.x = TRUE. In the continous case (with MLR), the
default is conditional.x = FALSE.

Yves.

